{
  "title": { "zh": "不接受自己的程序", "en": "Programs that reject themselves" },
  "after": { "zh": "L_s 不是<b>可识别语言</b>。", "en": "L_s is not a <b>recognisable language</b>." },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "u-ls",
      "kind": "proof",
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "r": "∃x. ∀y. M(x, c(y)) ↔ L(c(y))", "ls": "∀y. L(c(y)) ↔ ¬M(y, c(y))" }, "goal": "⊥" }],
      "cases": [{ "M": "Accepts", "L": "Ls" }],
      "brief": {
        "zh": "⟨y⟩ 是图灵机 y 的编码。L_s 装的是不接受自己编码的机器的编码。假设有一台机器 x 识别 L_s，推出矛盾 ⊥。",
        "en": "⟨y⟩ is the code of the Turing machine y. L_s holds the codes of machines that do not accept their own code. Supposing some machine x recognises L_s, get the contradiction ⊥."
      },
      "hint": [{ "zh": "让 x 读它自己的编码。", "en": "Let x read its own code." }],
      "solution": [
        "e = exE[x=a](r, body: l) {",
        "  body {",
        "    a2 = allE[t=a](ls)",
        "    a1 = allE[t=a](e.body)",
        "    s2 = andE(a2)",
        "    s1 = andE(a1)",
        "    c1 = chain(s1.left, s2.left)",
        "    c2 = chain(s2.right, s1.right)",
        "    j = andI(c1, c2)",
        "    l = liar(j)",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "goal <- e"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
